  "question": {
    "text": "Let the mean of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math> observations is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math>&nbsp;and the standard deviation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>. However, one observation was wrongly recorded. The sum of the correct and incorrect observations is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn></math>. If the mean of the correct set of observations is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math>, then the variance of the correct set is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>43</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>By using the formula of&nbsp;mean we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8721;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>750</mn></math></p><p>Now variance<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>15</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8721;</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>11450</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><munder><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mfenced><mi>new</mi></mfenced></munder><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mfenced><mi>new</mi></mfenced></munder><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8721;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>750</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math></p><p>Hence, if wrong observation was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;then corrected one is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn></math>.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, the correct observation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math>.</p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msup><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mfenced><mi>new</mi></mfenced></munder><mo>=</mo><mn>11450</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>10</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>60</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>14950</mn></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;variance of the correct set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>14950</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>16</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>299</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>256</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>43</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}